      "user_message": "Please remember that I spent time with my friend Emily last night discussing our upcoming trip to Italy.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and remember: Please remember that I spent time with my friend Emily last night discussing our upcoming trip to Italy.",
      "agent_response": "I can’t store personal memories long-term, but I can save or share this information for you. Which would you like me to do?\n\nOptions (pick one and tell me any details or recipient email):\n- Save a note to yourself (draft email to you) summarizing that you and Emily discussed the Italy trip and any action items.\n- Send or draft a message to Emily (I can send now or save as a draft). I’ll need Emily’s email if you want it sent.\n- Create a short checklist email for trip planning (dates, itinerary, packing, bookings) saved as a draft.\n- Create a quick text you can copy (social post or message).\n\nExample messages — tell me which to use or edit:\n1) To Emily (friendly follow-up):\n\"Hi Emily — great talking last night about our Italy trip! I’m excited to plan this with you. Do you want to confirm dates and start a shared packing/booking list? — [Your Name]\"\n\n2) Note to yourself (draft):\n\"Discussed upcoming trip to Italy with Emily last night. Action items: confirm travel dates, book flights/hotels, create packing list, research must-see sites.\"\n\n3) Quick social post:\n\"Had a great chat with my friend Emily last night — we’re planning a trip to Italy! Can’t wait to explore.\"\n\nTell me which action to take, any edits to the message, and (if sending) Emily’s email and whether to send now or save as draft.",
