      "agent_response": "I can’t store personal memories long‑term, but I can save or share this information for you. Which would you like me to do?\n\nOptions (pick one and give any details or recipient email):\n- Save a note to yourself (draft email to you) summarizing: “Tried a new restaurant with friends last Friday — had a blast exploring the menu.”\n- Send or draft a message to the friends who were there (need their email(s)).\n- Create a short social post you can copy/share.\n- Save a “memory” as a draft to refer back to later (subject and body I can prepare).\n\nExample messages — tell me which to use or edit:\n1) Note to self (draft subject/body):\nSubject: New restaurant — weekend visit\nBody: Tried a new restaurant with friends last Friday. We had a blast exploring the menu together. Remember to save the name, favorite dishes, and any photos.\n\n2) To friends:\n\"Hi — I had such a great time trying that new restaurant with you last Friday! Loved exploring the menu together — want to go back or try another place soon?\"\n\n3) Social post:\n\"Tried a new restaurant with friends last Friday — had a blast exploring the menu together!\"\n\nTell me which action you want and any edits. If you want me to send or save a draft, please provide the recipient email(s) and whether to send now or save.",
