      "agent_response": "Sounds lovely — glad you had fun!\n\nI can’t store it long‑term here, but I can save or share it for you. Which would you like me to do? Pick one and give any details (Jessica’s email if you want it sent):\n\nOptions\n- Send a quick thank-you/follow-up to Jessica now (need her email).\n- Save a draft to yourself summarizing the meetup (I’ll prepare a draft email).\n- Draft a message to plan trying the recipe together again.\n- Create a short social post you can copy/share.\n- Save a “memory” as a draft note you can refer to later.\n\nExample messages — tell me which to use or edit\n1) To Jessica (thank-you):\n\"Hi Jessica — I had a great time trying that new recipe with you at the cooking class last night! Want to get together soon to make it again or swap other recipes? — [Your Name]\"\n\n2) To Jessica (share photos/recipe):\n\"Hey Jessica — loved cooking with you last night! I took a photo of our dish and wrote down the recipe — want me to send it over?\"\n\n3) Note to self (draft):\n\"Cooking class with Jessica — tried a new recipe last night and had a great time. Follow-up: share recipe/photos, plan a cook-together.\"\n\nWhich action should I take, and any edits or recipient email?",
